# Herd local development

Laravel Herd serves this website locally. Cursor's `live-preview-gate` and `herd-local-preview` skills own the preview gate steps; this rule gives this repository's values. Herd's nginx serves `public/` through `LocalValetDriver.php`, which applies `public/.htaccess` as Cloudron's Apache does; PHP 8.4 runs any `.php` file, and Browsersync reloads the page on save. There is no database. Never use `file:///` as the preview.

| Slot | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Site | `http://apes-shelter-website.test` (Herd link `apes-shelter-website`, PHP 8.4) |
| Preview command | `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts\preview.ps1` (exit 0 ready, 1 blocked, 3 a decision) |
| Open in Cursor's browser | `http://localhost:3102` (Browsersync, proxying the site; UI on 3112) |
| Set up or repair | `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts\herd-setup.ps1` |
| Browsersync on its own | `npm run dev` |
| Site checks | `php scripts/check-site.php` |
| Version helper | `php scripts/milestone-version help` |

- Put Herd's PHP, Composer and Node first on `PATH` in agent shells: `$env:Path = "$env:USERPROFILE\.config\herd\bin;C:\Program Files\nodejs;$env:Path"`. `herd php` uses the site's isolated PHP 8.4.
- Profile values: `docs/herd/profile.json` (read by the scripts) and `docs/herd/profile.md`.
